[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3408062413","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111683#issuecomment-3408062413","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111683","id":3408062413,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LIufN","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T20:04:55Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T20:04:55Z","body":"That's expected behavior, although we don't seem to explain it in the documentation. Editor types are declared in the GodotSharpEditor assemblies which, as its name implies, is only available when running in the editor.\n\nTo exclude your `EditorToolExample` type from the export compilation, make sure to wrap it in `#if TOOLS` like the samples in the documentation:\n\n```csharp\n#if TOOLS\nusing Godot;\n\n[Tool]\n[GlobalClass]\npublic partial class EditorToolExample : EditorScript\n{\n\tpublic override void _Run()\n\t{\n\t\tGD.Print(\"Hello world!\");\n\t}\n}\n#endif\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3408062413/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3408363456","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111683#issuecomment-3408363456","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111683","id":3408363456,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LJ3_A","user":{"login":"GabCoolDude","id":123309403,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1mNWw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123309403?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude","html_url":"https://github.com/GabCoolDude","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T21:29:17Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T21:29:17Z","body":"> That's expected behavior, although we don't seem to explain it in the documentation.\n\nIt's not _explicitly_ mentioned, but all the code examples for making EditorPlugins use `#if TOOLS` (although not for EditorScript it seems). That should probably be changed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3408363456/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"